# DMA-BUF Flow

Shows the two paths for video frame handling: current CPU upload (Path B) and future zero-copy DMA-BUF (Path A).

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph PipeWire["PipeWire Screen Capture"]
        S[Screen capture source] --> F[Frame buffer]
    end

    subgraph Negotiation["DMA-BUF Capability Negotiation"]
        F --> N{Negotiate SPA_DATA_DmaBuf?}
        N -->|Success| MOD[Format + modifier fixation]
        N -->|Fallback| CPU_PATH
    end

    subgraph PathA["Path A: DMA-BUF (zero-copy, future)"]
        MOD --> IMPORT[Vulkan external memory import]
        IMPORT --> SYNC[Fence/semaphore sync]
        SYNC --> GPU_TEX[GPU texture from fd]
    end

    subgraph PathB["Path B: CPU upload (current)"]
        CPU_PATH["Copy frame to CPU buffer"]
        CPU_PATH --> CONV[Format conversion BGRx→RGBA]
        CONV --> UPLOAD[wgpu staging buffer upload]
        UPLOAD --> GPU_TEX2[GPU texture]
    end

    subgraph VideoManager["VideoManager"]
        GPU_TEX --> CACHE[Video texture cache]
        GPU_TEX2 --> CACHE
        CACHE --> LATEST{Latest-frame policy}
        LATEST -->|Active| VNODE[VideoNode]
        LATEST -->|Inactive| DROP[Discard]
    end

    subgraph Render["Rendering"]
        VNODE --> SCENE[Scene graph]
        SCENE --> RENDER[wgpu Renderer]
    end

    subgraph WaylandExport["Wayland Surface Export"]
        RENDER --> DMABUF_EXPORT["DMA-BUF export<br/>(wgpu → Wayland)"]
        DMABUF_EXPORT --> SURFACE[Wayland surface commit]
    end
```

# DMA-BUF Export (wgpu → Wayland)

Shows how the Dock renders to Wayland surfaces via DMA-BUF export. This is a different direction from the PipeWire DMA-BUF import.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Wgpu["wgpu Rendering"]
        DEVICE[wgpu Device] --> TEX["Create dmabuf-exportable texture"]
        TEX --> RENDER[wgpu-api render to texture]
        RENDER --> SUBMIT[Submit GPU command buffer]
    end

    subgraph Export["DMA-BUF Export"]
        SUBMIT --> EXPORT["wgpu_dmabuf::export()"]
        EXPORT --> PLANES[Extract dmabuf planes]
        PLANES --> FD[File descriptors per plane]
        FD --> STRIDE[Offset + stride per plane]
        STRIDE --> MODIFIER[DRM format modifier]
    end

    subgraph Wayland["Wayland Protocol"]
        MODIFIER --> PARAMS["zwp_linux_buffer_params_v1"]
        PARAMS --> BUFFER["Create wl_buffer"]
        BUFFER --> ATTACH["Attach to wl_surface"]
        ATTACH --> COMMIT["Commit surface"]
    end

    subgraph Compositor["Compositor"]
        COMMIT --> DISPLAY[Display on screen]
    end
```
